course: dictionary
lesson: 2171
title: Formal words in the news
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are formal, so you hear them in news reports and official papers more than in a chat with friends. «Correctional» is one of them. It describes places and work that punish people who broke the law and help them change.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «The new correctional facility opened on the edge of town.» A facility is a building made for a job, and the place is for people who have broken the law. So a correctional facility is a prison. Try your meaning in the sentence: "The new prison opened on the edge of town." It still makes sense, so the meaning fits.
explain: Official words can be different in different countries. In the US, «correctional facility» is the official word for a prison, and «correctional officer» is the official word for a prison guard. In Britain, people usually say prison and prison officer, so you will hear the word correctional mostly in North American texts.
fact: Correctional means to do with punishing people who broke the law and helping them change.
fact: «Correctional facility» is the US official word for a prison.
fact: «Correctional officer» is the US official word for a prison guard.
fact: You will mostly meet this word in news and formal texts from North America.
fact: When a word is formal, look at the words around it to find its meaning.
exercise: «The new correctional facility opened on the edge of town.» What is a correctional facility? | A school for very young children | A shop that sells maps | *A prison | A hospital for animals
exercise: A correctional officer works in a prison. What is a correctional officer? | *A prison guard | A doctor for sick animals | A chef who cooks for the children | A driver of school buses
exercise: A news writer uses «correctional facility» instead of prison. Why might they do this? | It means a park for families | It means a hospital, so it sounds kinder | It means a school, so it is easier to read | *It is a more formal name for a prison
test: Correctional describes a place that punishes people who broke the law and helps them change. Which place is correctional? | A football pitch | A library | *A prison | A bus station
test: A US news story says «correctional officer». Which job does this mean? | Bus driver | Park ranger | Dentist | *Prison guard
exam: «Correctional» means to do with punishing people who broke the law and helping them change. Which phrase is the US official word for a prison? | Village hall | Corrective glasses | *Correctional facility | Public library
